From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darius Mercadier <dmercadier@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:21:08 +0200
Subject: [compiler] Mark JSCreateGeneratorObject as writing and deoptimizing

Creating a generator object for a closure without an initial map calls
into the runtime to initialize its prototype and initial map. When the
new prototype is set up, JSObject::OptimizeAsPrototype can normalize
%GeneratorPrototype% from fast properties to dictionary mode, mutating
its map and invalidating stable-map dependencies.

Change JSCreateGeneratorObject from Operator::kEliminatable to
Operator::kNoThrow and give it a FrameState input so LoadElimination
does not eliminate map checks across it and lazy deoptimization has a
valid FrameState.

